An election to [[Three Rivers District Council]] took place on 5 May 2022. 14 of the 39 seats were up for election.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.threerivers.gov.uk/download?id=51839|title=Notice of Election – Three Rivers – Election of District Councillors|date=21 March 2022|access-date=3 April 2022|work=[[Three Rivers District Council]]|first=Joanne|last=Wagstaffe}}</ref> The election took place alongside [[2022 United Kingdom local elections|other local elections across the United Kingdom]].

==Background==
[[File:Three Rivers UK local election 2018 map.svg|thumb|150px|Result of the council election when these seats were last contested in 2018]]
[[File:2021 Three Rivers District Council election.svg|thumb|150px|Result of the most recent council election in 2021]]
The seats up for election in 2022 were those last contested in the [[2018 Three Rivers District Council election|2018 election]], when the [[Liberal Democrats (UK)|Liberal Democrats]] won eight seats, the [[Conservative Party (UK)|Conservatives]] won four seats, and [[Labour Party (UK)|Labour]] won one seat.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.threerivers.gov.uk/download?id=42085|title=District Council Election Results – May 2018|access-date=3 April 2022|work=[[Three Rivers District Council]]}}</ref> The Gade Valley ward elected two councillors in 2022 instead of one, due to the resignation of Independent (elected as a Liberal Democrat)<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.watfordobserver.co.uk/news/18497154.two-three-rivers-liberal-democrat-councillors-resign/|title=Two Three Rivers Liberal Democrat councillors resign|date=7 June 2020|access-date=3 April 2022|work=[[Watford Observer]]|first=Nathan|last=Louis}}</ref> councillor Alex Michaels in March 2022.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.threerivers.gov.uk/download?id=51833|title=Notice of Vacancy in Office of Councillor – Gade Valley Ward|date=18 March 2022|access-date=3 April 2022|work=[[Three Rivers District Council]]|first=Joanne|last=Wagstaffe}}</ref>

Following the elections of May 2022, Three Rivers District Council is controlled by the [[Liberal Democrats (UK)|Liberal Democrats]], who hold 23 of the 39 seats.<ref name="councillors">{{cite web|url=https://www.threerivers.gov.uk/listing/councillors|title=Councillors|access-date=3 April 2022|work=[[Three Rivers District Council]]}}</ref>

==Electoral process==
{{see also|Three Rivers District Council elections}}
Three Rivers District Council is elected in thirds, with a third of all seats up for election every year for three years, with an election to [[Hertfordshire County Council]] instead in the fourth year.<ref>{{cite web|url=https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/government/uploads/system/uploads/attachment_data/file/920186/Election_Timetable_in_England_2019.pdf|title=Election Timetable in England|access-date=3 April 2022|website=[[gov.uk]]}}</ref> The election took place by [[first-past-the-post voting]], with wards represented by three councillors, with one elected in each election year to serve a four-year term.

